        "id": 20381,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-11-11T19:21:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>First off, I already reported this through the feedback function in the game, so don't worry about that.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I was playing Ultimate Iron Legacy, with Writhe, Wraith, TLT, Guise, and Scholar.</p>\n<p>IL had Vigilance, Galvanized, and Demoralizing Presence. Writhe had the cloak.</p>\n<p>I played a card with Writhe, triggering the counter-attack from Vigilance. I discarded a card to prevent that damage.</p>\n<p>The game \"prevented\" that damage, but then applied the damage increase from Galvanized and Demoralizing Presence AFTER that, making him deal 2 damage (1 after the Cloak's reduction).</p>\n<p>For some reason, in this instance, it continued calculating damage after it was Prevented, which is obviously not how it is supposed to work.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:27.699Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
